{#- Implicit `limit self` at method boundaries (SPEC_0042 T3, SPEC_0034
    GAL-018/GAL-019): declared min/max ranges SATURATE — they are not Modelica
    assertions, nothing is signalled, and a qNaN stays a qNaN. The normative
    behaviour is `rumoca-eval-galec` (`execution.rs::limit_all`, reached from
    `interpreter.rs::invoke`): every INITIALIZED declared block variable
    (interface and protected), arrays elementwise, low bound applied before the
    high bound. These macros mirror that oracle statement for statement. An
    explicit GALEC `limit` statement is a different construct and keeps failing
    closed in the statements macro — T3 covers method boundaries only.

    Two facts this target owns and the oracle does not need:

    * **The numeric domain.** This target executes Real as binary32 and Integer
      as int32 (`c_type`, and the `[integer]` domain in `target.toml`), so a
      declared bound is decided in THAT domain, not in the f64/i64 the checked
      block carries it as. `binary32_bound` / `int32_bound` are the decision:
      each answers `none` when no value of the target type can violate the
      bound (elide the clamp — this is how a Modelica `min =
      -Modelica.Constants.inf` / `max = Modelica.Constants.inf` declaration
      reaches a target that cannot spell `1e60` as a `float`), a literal when
      the bound is representable, and fails closed when it is neither. This
      template picks the domain by naming those filters; the arithmetic is not
      re-derived here against a magic constant.
    * **Determinacy.** The block state is caller-allocated memory with no
      per-slot initialized flag, so the `Startup` RETURN boundary — the one
      boundary that runs before any other method has written anything — clamps
      only what `Startup` is proven to have written
      (`startup.definite_state_writes`). That mirrors the oracle skipping an
      uninitialized slot, and it is what keeps a declared range on a control
      input (which `Startup` never assigns) from making the generated code read
      indeterminate memory. Every later boundary limits the full state. -#}
